1 INTRODUCTION
Several applications at the frontier of databases (DBs) and machine
learning (ML) require support for query processing over ML mod-
els. In image retrieval for instance, querying a DB corresponds to
finding images whose neural representations are close to an input
query image, given a distance measure [ 28,29]. Similarly, in the
medical domain, a typical query would look for patients whose
