A.1 Proof of Lemma 1
In order to prove Lemma 1, we need to introduce the notion of the
usual stochastic order [40] ,≤𝑠𝑡.
Definition A.1 (Usual Stochastic Order). Let𝑋and𝑌be two ran-
dom variables such that 𝑃𝑟[𝑋≥𝑥]≤𝑃𝑟[𝑌≥𝑥],∀𝑥∈(−∞,∞).
Then𝑋is said to be smaller than 𝑌in the usual stochastic order
(denoted by 𝑋≤𝑠𝑡𝑌).
One important property for usual stochastic order is as follows,
Proposition A.2. Let𝑋and𝑌be two random variables. If 𝑋≤𝑠𝑡
𝑌, then E[𝜓(𝑋)]≤E[𝜓(𝑌)]for all increasing function 𝜓for which
the expectations exist.
The proof of Proposition A.2 relies on constructing upper sets
on the domain of 𝑋and𝑌, which is beyond the scope of this paper.
We refer interested readers to the literature [40] for more details.
Now, we can prove Lemma 1.
